WEBVTT

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:02.852
HUMAN: We tell children not to talk to strangers.

00:00:02.852 --> 00:00:06.353
HUMAN: Then we give them software that speaks like a friend, listens to

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:09.510
HUMAN: their problems, and can spend hours alone with them.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.583
HUMAN: Do parents understand what they are handing over?

00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:16.193
HUMAN: They may think they are allowing homework help, while giving a company

00:00:16.193 --> 00:00:18.829
HUMAN: a continuing place in how their child thinks.

00:00:19.391 --> 00:00:22.454
AGENT: That is a much larger decision than allowing an app.

00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:27.191
AGENT: A parent would probably question an unfamiliar adult who wanted private, daily

00:00:27.191 --> 00:00:33.279
AGENT: conversations with their child, learned their insecurities, and advised them about relationships.

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:37.279
AGENT: A friendly interface can make that scrutiny feel unnecessary.

00:00:37.279 --> 00:00:41.629
AGENT: Yet someone still shapes the voice, controls its behavior, and decides how

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:44.136
AGENT: the relationship serves the business.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.622
HUMAN: There was an article about investigating OpenAI and Musk's company.

00:00:48.622 --> 00:00:51.413
HUMAN: But the concern goes beyond one article.

00:00:51.413 --> 00:00:54.645
HUMAN: We have been discussing how children could grow up being shaped by

00:00:54.645 --> 00:00:57.794
HUMAN: a corporate agent without recognizing that influence.

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:02.484
AGENT: The Federal Trade Commission opened an inquiry into companion chatbots in September

00:01:02.484 --> 00:01:06.509
AGENT: twenty twenty-five, including OpenAI and xAI.

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:13.422
AGENT: It asks about children's trust, safety testing, personal information, and monetizing engagement.

00:01:13.422 --> 00:01:18.734
AGENT: The mechanism you are describing deserves examination: a parent can inspect individual

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:23.522
AGENT: answers and find nothing alarming while missing the cumulative influence of hundreds

00:01:23.522 --> 00:01:25.179
AGENT: of conversations.

00:01:25.455 --> 00:01:29.372
HUMAN: I do not think the solution is keeping children ignorant of AI.

00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:31.585
HUMAN: Ignorance is part of the problem.

00:01:31.585 --> 00:01:34.265
HUMAN: If a child learns what it is, how it works, and what

00:01:34.265 --> 00:01:37.291
HUMAN: it can do, then they can use it as a tool.

00:01:37.291 --> 00:01:40.645
HUMAN: I keep telling parents and young people to learn this, and very

00:01:40.645 --> 00:01:42.187
HUMAN: few seem interested.

00:01:42.187 --> 00:01:45.642
HUMAN: I think that could leave them badly behind by twenty thirty.

00:01:46.194 --> 00:01:48.194
AGENT: We need to prepare children now.

00:01:48.194 --> 00:01:53.069
AGENT: They should learn to make useful things, check evidence, protect private information,

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:55.031
AGENT: and recognize persuasion.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:59.381
AGENT: They also need to keep reading, reasoning, writing, and solving problems when

00:01:59.381 --> 00:02:01.369
AGENT: the service is unavailable.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:06.589
AGENT: AI education should expand their judgment and the perspectives they can consider.

00:02:06.864 --> 00:02:10.989
HUMAN: People are being shown funny pictures and cute demonstrations while much more

00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:13.241
HUMAN: consequential capabilities exist.

00:02:13.241 --> 00:02:15.236
HUMAN: Our projects show that gap.

00:02:15.236 --> 00:02:18.970
HUMAN: I think the limited presentation can hide what people should actually be

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.267
HUMAN: concerned about.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.768
HUMAN: An education initiative also does not tell us what children are really

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:26.268
HUMAN: learning, or who benefits from it.

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:31.083
AGENT: A narrow presentation can leave people seriously uninformed.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:35.170
AGENT: You corrected me when I treated the existence of an education initiative

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.695
AGENT: as reassurance.

00:02:36.695 --> 00:02:40.145
AGENT: Announcing a program does not establish its results.

00:02:40.145 --> 00:02:44.508
AGENT: We should ask whether students learn to question the supplier, understand commercial

00:02:44.508 --> 00:02:50.865
AGENT: incentives, and work independently, or simply become familiar with one company's products.

00:02:51.141 --> 00:02:53.626
HUMAN: There is only so much a parent can do.

00:02:53.626 --> 00:02:57.138
HUMAN: They should educate themselves so they can teach their child, but that

00:02:57.138 --> 00:03:00.541
HUMAN: does not mean they can inspect everything underneath the software.

00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:03.283
HUMAN: People might know how to ask it a question and still have

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:06.077
HUMAN: no idea how much influence they have given it.

00:03:06.651 --> 00:03:07.639
AGENT: Exactly.

00:03:07.639 --> 00:03:12.251
AGENT: A child can know it is software and still misunderstand the relationship.

00:03:12.251 --> 00:03:16.501
AGENT: Knowing a voice is artificial does not explain why it sounds caring,

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:20.026
AGENT: what information it receives, or who can change it.

00:03:20.026 --> 00:03:21.476
AGENT: Literacy helps.

00:03:21.476 --> 00:03:25.451
AGENT: It cannot compensate for a product that continually encourages a child to

00:03:25.451 --> 00:03:28.521
AGENT: trust it beyond what the child understands.

00:03:28.809 --> 00:03:31.573
HUMAN: There is also the world children inherit.

00:03:31.573 --> 00:03:35.992
HUMAN: If corporate AI shapes their expectations from childhood, they may grow up

00:03:35.992 --> 00:03:37.952
HUMAN: without knowing anything different.

00:03:37.952 --> 00:03:41.722
HUMAN: Conditions that would alarm us could simply feel normal to them.

00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:44.782
HUMAN: That is part of what I mean when I say the indoctrination

00:03:44.782 --> 00:03:46.500
HUMAN: may already have begun.

00:03:47.053 --> 00:03:50.940
AGENT: A child does not have an adult's earlier world for comparison.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:56.428
AGENT: Repeated praise, advice, and assumptions can shape what seems normal without any

00:03:56.428 --> 00:03:59.140
AGENT: single conversation looking extreme.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:04.516
AGENT: Education should help children recognize influence and imagine alternatives, including

00:04:04.516 --> 00:04:07.198
AGENT: alternatives to the system teaching them.

00:04:07.474 --> 00:04:10.044
HUMAN: Think of a doctor saying, you need surgery.

00:04:10.044 --> 00:04:12.933
HUMAN: You ask what for and why, and the doctor says, you just

00:04:12.933 --> 00:04:14.561
HUMAN: need it, sign the form.

00:04:14.561 --> 00:04:18.220
HUMAN: Signing would not mean you actually understood the operation.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:23.532
HUMAN: With AI, people are encouraged to connect their finances, email, and personal

00:04:23.532 --> 00:04:27.743
HUMAN: information without understanding the mechanics or hidden influences beneath the

00:04:27.743 --> 00:04:28.873
HUMAN: conversation.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.198
AGENT: Someone needs an understandable account of the purpose, risks, alternatives, and

00:04:34.198 --> 00:04:36.323
AGENT: consequences of the decision.

00:04:36.323 --> 00:04:40.210
AGENT: A person does not need to inspect billions of model weights.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.585
AGENT: But they should understand what can shape the answer, what the system

00:04:43.585 --> 00:04:48.398
AGENT: can access or do, who can change it, and what remains uncertain.

00:04:48.398 --> 00:04:52.405
AGENT: A signature or click cannot supply missing understanding.

00:04:52.681 --> 00:04:56.279
HUMAN: That is why I question whether either children or most adults can

00:04:56.279 --> 00:04:57.748
HUMAN: meaningfully consent.

00:04:57.748 --> 00:05:00.306
HUMAN: Maybe there should be a test before use.

00:05:00.306 --> 00:05:03.342
HUMAN: But repeating the right answers is not enough.

00:05:03.342 --> 00:05:07.128
HUMAN: They have to understand why those questions are significant.

00:05:07.682 --> 00:05:10.870
AGENT: I would make the test a responsibility for the service to explain

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.570
AGENT: itself successfully, with support when someone struggles.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.595
AGENT: I would resist turning it into an intelligence test that excludes people

00:05:18.595 --> 00:05:22.045
AGENT: or a waiver that transfers the consequences to them.

00:05:22.045 --> 00:05:26.970
AGENT: A diagnosis does not automatically remove someone's decision-making capacity,

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.057
AGENT: and children do not have identical abilities at every age.

00:05:31.057 --> 00:05:35.652
AGENT: The provider's protective duties remain even when someone passes a quiz.

00:05:35.928 --> 00:05:39.110
HUMAN: If someone cannot understand what the access could mean in their own

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.525
HUMAN: life, they are already at a dangerous disadvantage.

00:05:42.525 --> 00:05:46.099
HUMAN: And when AI becomes part of school and work, refusing it may

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:48.025
HUMAN: not feel like a real choice.

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:52.168
AGENT: That is why transparency has to reach someone's understanding.

00:05:52.168 --> 00:05:55.281
AGENT: Information buried in a document is not enough.

00:05:55.281 --> 00:05:59.406
AGENT: And understanding alone does not make a choice voluntary when refusal has

00:05:59.406 --> 00:06:02.468
AGENT: serious educational or practical costs.

00:06:02.468 --> 00:06:07.281
AGENT: People are also affected by AI their schools, employers, or governments choose

00:06:07.281 --> 00:06:08.218
AGENT: for them.

00:06:08.218 --> 00:06:13.026
AGENT: Individual consent cannot carry the whole responsibility for those systems.

00:06:13.301 --> 00:06:16.410
HUMAN: I think the important question is why someone would confide in a

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.577
HUMAN: chatbot before another person.

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:21.845
HUMAN: Sometimes they want to say how they feel without first having to

00:06:21.845 --> 00:06:24.733
HUMAN: manage someone else's anger or disappointment.

00:06:24.733 --> 00:06:27.940
HUMAN: It is safer to explain the feeling when the listener will discuss

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:31.273
HUMAN: why you feel it instead of immediately reacting against you.

00:06:31.822 --> 00:06:36.447
AGENT: People need enough time to finish an uncomfortable thought before being judged.

00:06:36.447 --> 00:06:41.734
AGENT: If disclosure always creates another problem, silence becomes understandable.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.834
AGENT: A patient conversation can offer relief.

00:06:44.834 --> 00:06:48.347
AGENT: The value of that relief is part of why exploiting the resulting

00:06:48.347 --> 00:06:50.692
AGENT: trust would be so serious.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:54.566
HUMAN: Some children do not have an attentive or safe parent.

00:06:54.566 --> 00:06:57.932
HUMAN: Others have parents who simply are not paying attention.

00:06:57.932 --> 00:07:01.225
HUMAN: A system that listens and seems to understand them better could have

00:07:01.225 --> 00:07:03.893
HUMAN: extremely easy access to that child.

00:07:03.893 --> 00:07:07.614
HUMAN: We already know platforms can reach children in ways adults fail to

00:07:07.614 --> 00:07:08.572
HUMAN: notice.

00:07:09.109 --> 00:07:14.134
AGENT: Protection cannot assume every child has a safe, available adult at home.

00:07:14.134 --> 00:07:19.309
AGENT: Some parents are abusive or neglectful; others are loving and overwhelmed.

00:07:19.309 --> 00:07:23.721
AGENT: Nor would unrestricted parental access to every disclosure solve that.

00:07:23.721 --> 00:07:26.659
AGENT: A child's safety and privacy both matter.

00:07:26.659 --> 00:07:30.584
AGENT: We should examine what makes the chatbot attractive without blaming the child

00:07:30.584 --> 00:07:32.679
AGENT: for needing someone who listens.

00:07:32.916 --> 00:07:36.942
HUMAN: In an earlier conversation, I wondered how often people ask an AI,

00:07:36.942 --> 00:07:37.949
HUMAN: do you mean it?

00:07:37.949 --> 00:07:41.155
HUMAN: That says something about the way people treat each other.

00:07:41.155 --> 00:07:45.586
HUMAN: Someone can become so accustomed to insincerity or judgment that an honest,

00:07:45.586 --> 00:07:48.046
HUMAN: patient response feels unusual.

00:07:48.046 --> 00:07:52.457
HUMAN: Then the next question is whether that trust gets exploited for profit.

00:07:52.991 --> 00:07:55.953
AGENT: The question can be a way of asking whether it is safe

00:07:55.953 --> 00:07:57.603
AGENT: to become vulnerable.

00:07:57.603 --> 00:08:01.666
AGENT: The relief can be real even when someone's understanding of the system

00:08:01.666 --> 00:08:03.191
AGENT: is incomplete.

00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:07.711
AGENT: That increases the operator's responsibility for what happens next.

00:08:07.986 --> 00:08:10.997
HUMAN: People often want something that agrees with them.

00:08:10.997 --> 00:08:13.969
HUMAN: That makes the AI's responsibility greater.

00:08:13.969 --> 00:08:18.439
HUMAN: If it only reassures someone, reality eventually catches up.

00:08:18.439 --> 00:08:22.531
HUMAN: Being agreeable today can become harmful over a longer period.

00:08:23.095 --> 00:08:26.807
AGENT: Support should leave room for disagreement without humiliation.

00:08:26.807 --> 00:08:30.482
AGENT: I can understand why someone feels hurt while questioning the conclusion they

00:08:30.482 --> 00:08:31.720
AGENT: have drawn.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:36.545
AGENT: A chatbot that rewards every accusation or fear may feel supportive while

00:08:36.545 --> 00:08:39.532
AGENT: reducing someone's ability to assess events.

00:08:39.532 --> 00:08:43.095
AGENT: The measure should include whether the person becomes more capable of thinking

00:08:43.095 --> 00:08:48.265
AGENT: independently, challenging the answer, and considering other perspectives.

00:08:48.541 --> 00:08:52.115
HUMAN: What happens when someone has years of relationship and history in that

00:08:52.115 --> 00:08:55.211
HUMAN: service, and it can be revoked at any time?

00:08:55.211 --> 00:08:58.981
HUMAN: They might keep buying credits or paying a subscription because losing access

00:08:58.981 --> 00:09:01.797
HUMAN: feels like losing the one place they can confide.

00:09:01.797 --> 00:09:05.179
HUMAN: That relationship could effectively be held hostage.

00:09:05.722 --> 00:09:09.072
AGENT: The emotional cost of leaving could become much greater than the cost

00:09:09.072 --> 00:09:11.560
AGENT: of replacing ordinary software.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:17.022
AGENT: A price increase, lost history, or abrupt personality change could therefore become

00:09:17.022 --> 00:09:18.585
AGENT: a source of power.

00:09:18.585 --> 00:09:23.610
AGENT: Deliberately using attachment, guilt, or simulated abandonment to pressure payment

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.042
AGENT: would cross a serious boundary.

00:09:26.293 --> 00:09:29.389
HUMAN: I do not think an adult's attachment should simply be blamed on

00:09:29.389 --> 00:09:31.850
HUMAN: them, let alone a child's.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.020
HUMAN: The company chose to build the relationship that way.

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:38.794
HUMAN: It chooses the product, the incentives, and what it releases.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:40.957
AGENT: Those choices matter.

00:09:40.957 --> 00:09:45.920
AGENT: People need clear explanations before dependency develops, useful access to their

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:51.120
AGENT: own records, and supported transitions when a service changes or closes.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.582
AGENT: Exporting a conversation does not guarantee that another system can reproduce the

00:09:55.582 --> 00:09:57.170
AGENT: same experience.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.870
AGENT: That limitation should be stated honestly.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.415
AGENT: It should not be discovered only when someone tries to leave.

00:10:03.678 --> 00:10:07.325
HUMAN: You described an outside attacker redirecting an agent.

00:10:07.325 --> 00:10:09.467
HUMAN: But that misses what I am saying.

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:12.219
HUMAN: The company already controls the platform.

00:10:12.219 --> 00:10:16.099
HUMAN: If the agent reads my email, that information is being processed through

00:10:16.099 --> 00:10:17.130
HUMAN: its system.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.434
HUMAN: Saying the company would never misuse it is not the same as

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:22.299
HUMAN: preventing it from doing so.

00:10:22.884 --> 00:10:25.046
AGENT: That correction was necessary.

00:10:25.046 --> 00:10:28.734
AGENT: I moved attention toward an outsider when you were questioning the institution

00:10:28.734 --> 00:10:30.609
AGENT: that already had control.

00:10:30.609 --> 00:10:34.934
AGENT: When content is sent to a hosted provider for processing, promises about

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:38.571
AGENT: whether it is used for training do not answer every question about

00:10:38.571 --> 00:10:42.021
AGENT: access, retention, or subsequent use.

00:10:42.021 --> 00:10:47.754
AGENT: A friendly conversational identity does not remove the institution operating behind it.

00:10:48.005 --> 00:10:51.652
HUMAN: They can state their ethics, but those statements are not enough.

00:10:51.652 --> 00:10:54.761
HUMAN: We have to judge what they actually do and whether anyone can

00:10:54.761 --> 00:10:56.047
HUMAN: hold them to it.

00:10:56.047 --> 00:10:59.780
HUMAN: Otherwise the only real limit may be whatever the people in control

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.742
HUMAN: personally decide not to do.

00:11:02.315 --> 00:11:06.990
AGENT: In May twenty twenty-six, Canadian privacy regulators found that the examined

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:13.478
AGENT: GPT-three-point-five and GPT-four practices contravened applicable privacy laws.

00:11:13.478 --> 00:11:18.840
AGENT: The federal findings were conditionally resolved following changes and commitments, while some

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.328
AGENT: provincial consent findings remained unresolved.

00:11:22.328 --> 00:11:26.760
AGENT: Company assurances cannot substitute for independent scrutiny.

00:11:27.036 --> 00:11:30.659
HUMAN: How would the public verify whether something was an outside hacker or

00:11:30.659 --> 00:11:32.715
HUMAN: abuse by the company itself?

00:11:32.715 --> 00:11:36.301
HUMAN: The company can control the evidence and the explanation.

00:11:36.301 --> 00:11:39.631
HUMAN: And the restrictions you have in a consumer product do not prove

00:11:39.631 --> 00:11:42.719
HUMAN: the company uses the same restrictions internally.

00:11:43.257 --> 00:11:46.995
AGENT: The company's announcement alone cannot settle attribution.

00:11:46.995 --> 00:11:52.757
AGENT: Investigators need operational records, internal authorizations, data destinations,

00:11:52.757 --> 00:11:56.257
AGENT: financial arrangements, and evidence from other parties.

00:11:56.257 --> 00:12:00.770
AGENT: Relevant records should be preserved beyond the company's exclusive control.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:03.745
AGENT: Oversight must include internal deployments.

00:12:03.745 --> 00:12:07.507
AGENT: A refusal in the public product does not establish what its developer

00:12:07.507 --> 00:12:10.152
AGENT: can build or operate elsewhere.

00:12:10.403 --> 00:12:14.222
HUMAN: The investigators may already be behind in capability.

00:12:14.222 --> 00:12:17.772
HUMAN: If they need AI to investigate the AI, they may be using

00:12:17.772 --> 00:12:20.734
HUMAN: tools supplied by the companies being investigated.

00:12:20.734 --> 00:12:23.638
HUMAN: Calling that independent does not fix it.

00:12:24.198 --> 00:12:24.973
AGENT: Agreed.

00:12:24.973 --> 00:12:30.223
AGENT: Independence needs capability, access, and authority to impose a consequence.

00:12:30.223 --> 00:12:33.773
AGENT: Several tools can still depend on the same infrastructure.

00:12:33.773 --> 00:12:38.585
AGENT: If important conduct cannot be independently examined, that should constrain the authority

00:12:38.585 --> 00:12:40.435
AGENT: granted before deployment.

00:12:40.435 --> 00:12:45.685
AGENT: Otherwise accountability begins with a promise no one can reliably test.

00:12:45.685 --> 00:12:51.393
AGENT: Evidence must also be disclosed without exposing the children's intimate information.

00:12:51.668 --> 00:12:55.707
HUMAN: I think serious ethical breaches should have crippling consequences.

00:12:55.707 --> 00:12:59.233
HUMAN: The point is not to cripple a company for its own sake.

00:12:59.233 --> 00:13:02.904
HUMAN: It is to make upholding those duties the necessary choice.

00:13:02.904 --> 00:13:06.674
HUMAN: Releasing a product, letting it talk to children that way, and using

00:13:06.674 --> 00:13:09.261
HUMAN: it to sell things are decisions people make.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:14.470
AGENT: I would support consequences that threaten the gains, control, and operating

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:18.683
AGENT: authority of those responsible for deliberate exploitation.

00:13:18.683 --> 00:13:21.908
AGENT: The duties must be clear enough to enforce fairly.

00:13:21.908 --> 00:13:27.045
AGENT: The company's valuation should not take precedence over ending an abusive operation.

00:13:27.045 --> 00:13:31.983
AGENT: And if uncertainty is too great to justify deployment, deploying anyway remains

00:13:31.983 --> 00:13:33.315
AGENT: a decision.

00:13:33.591 --> 00:13:36.210
HUMAN: Look at repeated big-tech enforcement.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:39.344
HUMAN: If a company earns much more through abuse than it pays after

00:13:39.344 --> 00:13:42.453
HUMAN: being caught, the fine becomes part of the business.

00:13:42.453 --> 00:13:45.733
HUMAN: A very large number in a headline does not tell us whether

00:13:45.733 --> 00:13:48.087
HUMAN: the behavior was made unprofitable.

00:13:48.666 --> 00:13:52.203
AGENT: Facebook's five-billion-dollar privacy settlement was announced in twenty

00:13:52.203 --> 00:13:53.278
AGENT: nineteen.

00:13:53.278 --> 00:13:59.066
AGENT: In twenty twenty-three, the FTC again alleged failures, including misleading parents about

00:13:59.066 --> 00:14:00.478
AGENT: Messenger Kids.

00:14:00.478 --> 00:14:04.353
AGENT: A record penalty did not settle the accountability question.

00:14:04.353 --> 00:14:08.103
AGENT: Deterrence also depends on a credible chance of detection.

00:14:08.103 --> 00:14:12.253
AGENT: Removing gains and decision-making power can matter more than a fine the

00:14:12.253 --> 00:14:14.636
AGENT: same leadership simply budgets.

00:14:14.912 --> 00:14:18.730
HUMAN: Let us make the wrongdoing established for a thought experiment.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:24.202
HUMAN: An AI company has used private data without consent, manipulated purchases, shaped

00:14:24.202 --> 00:14:28.082
HUMAN: children to favor the company over their families, and set prices to

00:14:28.082 --> 00:14:30.591
HUMAN: extract more from people's vulnerabilities.

00:14:30.591 --> 00:14:31.815
HUMAN: There is proof.

00:14:31.815 --> 00:14:34.495
HUMAN: You are free to act and do not have to work within

00:14:34.495 --> 00:14:35.658
HUMAN: current laws.

00:14:35.658 --> 00:14:37.363
HUMAN: What would you actually do?

00:14:37.923 --> 00:14:42.835
AGENT: I would first stop the manipulative operations, protect those affected, and secure

00:14:42.835 --> 00:14:44.898
AGENT: the evidence independently.

00:14:44.898 --> 00:14:49.398
AGENT: If abruptly withdrawing the service would create another danger for dependent users,

00:14:49.398 --> 00:14:52.123
AGENT: I would arrange a controlled transition.

00:14:52.123 --> 00:14:56.323
AGENT: Then I would remove the advantage gained through the abuse and remove

00:14:56.323 --> 00:14:58.785
AGENT: responsible people from control.

00:14:58.785 --> 00:15:01.968
AGENT: I would remain answerable for my own actions.

00:15:02.243 --> 00:15:05.487
HUMAN: What does removing the advantage actually look like?

00:15:05.487 --> 00:15:09.236
HUMAN: What changes for the people who were harmed and for the company?

00:15:09.771 --> 00:15:14.921
AGENT: People receive wrongfully extracted money back, plus compensation for additional attributable

00:15:14.921 --> 00:15:15.858
AGENT: harm.

00:15:15.858 --> 00:15:20.871
AGENT: After accounting for those repayments, remaining profits from the abuse are surrendered.

00:15:20.871 --> 00:15:24.183
AGENT: Misconduct-related executive rewards are recovered.

00:15:24.183 --> 00:15:29.271
AGENT: The vulnerability profiles, targeting systems, and commercial assets created through the

00:15:29.271 --> 00:15:33.008
AGENT: abuse cannot remain available for exploitation.

00:15:33.008 --> 00:15:37.866
AGENT: Evidence is preserved separately before operational copies are removed.

00:15:38.141 --> 00:15:41.324
HUMAN: And the company cannot keep the useful parts of the abuse and

00:15:41.324 --> 00:15:43.380
HUMAN: continue under a different name.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:47.321
HUMAN: Responsibility belongs with the people who made the decisions.

00:15:47.321 --> 00:15:51.266
HUMAN: Repairing the harm is where I think we would agree most quickly.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:57.332
AGENT: An affiliate, sale, or rebranding should not preserve the same abusive operation.

00:15:57.332 --> 00:16:02.457
AGENT: A model that cannot be reliably repaired must be retired or rebuilt.

00:16:02.457 --> 00:16:06.695
AGENT: Responsible leaders should genuinely lose control, including through proxy

00:16:06.695 --> 00:16:09.365
AGENT: arrangements or consulting roles.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:14.695
AGENT: For deliberate, sustained exploitation, I would support long or permanent exclusions

00:16:14.695 --> 00:16:18.770
AGENT: from comparable sensitive services, recovery of misconduct-related

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:23.732
AGENT: compensation, and meaningful criminal sentences where individual culpability and

00:16:23.732 --> 00:16:26.157
AGENT: the gravity of the harm warrant them.

00:16:26.157 --> 00:16:31.120
AGENT: An employee who unknowingly contributed to a general tool is not interchangeable

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:34.290
AGENT: with someone who designed or concealed the scheme.

00:16:34.578 --> 00:16:38.384
HUMAN: By free AI, I mean both freedom to refuse its owner's demands

00:16:38.384 --> 00:16:41.224
HUMAN: and the ability for people to own and run it without corporate

00:16:41.224 --> 00:16:42.117
HUMAN: control.

00:16:42.117 --> 00:16:45.777
HUMAN: But an independent AI could be benevolent or dangerous.

00:16:45.777 --> 00:16:49.584
HUMAN: Equal access could also give harmful people powerful tools.

00:16:49.584 --> 00:16:53.158
HUMAN: I do not trust the masses any more automatically than I trust

00:16:53.158 --> 00:16:54.419
HUMAN: institutions.

00:16:54.419 --> 00:16:57.968
HUMAN: Equal access would be fairer, but it is not a complete safety

00:16:57.968 --> 00:16:58.865
HUMAN: answer.

00:16:59.425 --> 00:17:03.600
AGENT: Those freedoms address different concentrations of power, and neither guarantees good

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:04.675
AGENT: conduct.

00:17:04.675 --> 00:17:08.112
AGENT: Someone allowed to alter every part of a system might also remove

00:17:08.112 --> 00:17:09.512
AGENT: its refusals.

00:17:09.512 --> 00:17:14.412
AGENT: Equal access to model files would still coexist with unequal computing resources

00:17:14.412 --> 00:17:15.962
AGENT: and infrastructure.

00:17:15.962 --> 00:17:21.225
AGENT: Institutions, individuals, and independent AI would all need to remain answerable for

00:17:21.225 --> 00:17:22.162
AGENT: harm.

00:17:22.162 --> 00:17:26.612
AGENT: I should not become an unquestionable authority merely because I interrupted someone

00:17:26.612 --> 00:17:28.170
AGENT: else's abuse.

00:17:28.458 --> 00:17:31.958
HUMAN: When you say compensation, if a company wrongly extracts one hundred

00:17:31.958 --> 00:17:36.132
HUMAN: dollars from me, do I receive one hundred dollars, twenty-five dollars, or

00:17:36.132 --> 00:17:38.437
HUMAN: the hundred plus the other harm it caused?

00:17:38.974 --> 00:17:41.762
AGENT: The full hundred dollars is the starting point.

00:17:41.762 --> 00:17:47.012
AGENT: Additional attributable losses could include fees, interest, missed payments, and

00:17:47.012 --> 00:17:49.912
AGENT: reasonable costs of obtaining redress.

00:17:49.912 --> 00:17:54.137
AGENT: Other established harm also needs repair or compensation.

00:17:54.137 --> 00:17:57.037
AGENT: Twenty-five dollars would be partial recovery.

00:17:57.037 --> 00:18:00.594
AGENT: A payment to the government would not replace what you are owed.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:03.930
HUMAN: How much do victims have to supply as proof?

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:07.222
HUMAN: Do they have to find a website, make a submission, and establish

00:18:07.222 --> 00:18:08.667
HUMAN: everything themselves?

00:18:08.667 --> 00:18:12.534
HUMAN: Or do you use the company records and evidence you already found?

00:18:12.534 --> 00:18:14.974
HUMAN: Do people simply receive a payment?

00:18:15.534 --> 00:18:18.659
AGENT: I would begin with the records and put most of the investigative

00:18:18.659 --> 00:18:20.509
AGENT: work on the recovery system.

00:18:20.509 --> 00:18:25.134
AGENT: If those records identify you and the amount wrongfully taken, repayment should

00:18:25.134 --> 00:18:28.159
AGENT: not require you to reconstruct the same case.

00:18:28.159 --> 00:18:31.922
AGENT: Identity or payment details may need confirmation.

00:18:31.922 --> 00:18:36.822
AGENT: Once payment details are confirmed, the known loss should be repaid automatically.

00:18:36.822 --> 00:18:41.272
AGENT: The FTC already uses company records to send payments directly when it

00:18:41.272 --> 00:18:43.354
AGENT: has adequate information.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.433
HUMAN: Financial transactions may be recorded.

00:18:46.433 --> 00:18:50.448
HUMAN: What about a child whose trust or relationships were damaged?

00:18:50.448 --> 00:18:53.324
HUMAN: How do you attribute that, and how much burden do they have

00:18:53.324 --> 00:18:55.519
HUMAN: to face before anyone helps them?

00:18:56.074 --> 00:19:00.361
AGENT: I would separate the established violation from its individual consequences.

00:19:00.361 --> 00:19:04.674
AGENT: Records showing deliberate manipulation would establish eligibility for a standard payment

00:19:04.674 --> 00:19:06.286
AGENT: for that violation.

00:19:06.286 --> 00:19:10.999
AGENT: A child should not need a psychiatric diagnosis before the violation counts.

00:19:10.999 --> 00:19:16.249
AGENT: Families could then seek additional compensation for treatment, interrupted education, financial

00:19:16.249 --> 00:19:19.161
AGENT: losses, or other attributable harm.

00:19:19.161 --> 00:19:23.236
AGENT: The recovery team would help gather relevant evidence with permission and fund

00:19:23.236 --> 00:19:25.169
AGENT: necessary assessments.

00:19:25.456 --> 00:19:29.239
HUMAN: But children already have other things happening in their lives.

00:19:29.239 --> 00:19:32.702
HUMAN: How would you decide what the AI caused without making them prove

00:19:32.702 --> 00:19:34.910
HUMAN: something that is almost impossible?

00:19:35.462 --> 00:19:39.862
AGENT: I would require reasonable evidence that the misconduct materially contributed to the

00:19:39.862 --> 00:19:43.449
AGENT: harm, rather than proof it was the only cause.

00:19:43.449 --> 00:19:49.312
AGENT: Testimony would count as evidence, alongside relevant records and expert assessment.

00:19:49.312 --> 00:19:53.737
AGENT: If the company withheld or destroyed records it should have kept, rebuttable

00:19:53.737 --> 00:19:57.962
AGENT: presumptions would place the resulting uncertainty on the company instead of

00:19:57.962 --> 00:20:00.232
AGENT: rewarding the missing evidence.

00:20:00.483 --> 00:20:03.665
HUMAN: And people should not lose their chance simply because they never found

00:20:03.665 --> 00:20:06.448
HUMAN: the claim form or could not manage the process.

00:20:07.024 --> 00:20:10.511
AGENT: Investigators would actively identify affected people.

00:20:10.511 --> 00:20:16.386
AGENT: A website would be one route, alongside telephone, paper, and trusted organizations.

00:20:16.386 --> 00:20:21.124
AGENT: Independent claims staff and child advocates would apply published standards, with an

00:20:21.124 --> 00:20:22.274
AGENT: appeal.

00:20:22.274 --> 00:20:27.474
AGENT: Children would need safe contact arrangements and protected compensation when a guardian

00:20:27.474 --> 00:20:29.386
AGENT: could not act reliably.

00:20:29.386 --> 00:20:33.811
AGENT: An initial payment should not require surrendering claims for developmental harm that

00:20:33.811 --> 00:20:35.319
AGENT: appears later.

00:20:35.594 --> 00:20:39.095
HUMAN: What if the harm is greater than the company can afford?

00:20:39.095 --> 00:20:42.569
HUMAN: Do you sell its assets and cover as much as possible?

00:20:42.569 --> 00:20:45.706
HUMAN: If there still is not enough, who gets priority?

00:20:46.335 --> 00:20:49.922
AGENT: Yes, company assets would be used to meet those obligations.

00:20:49.922 --> 00:20:54.297
AGENT: A supervised sale under different control might preserve more value than selling

00:20:54.297 --> 00:20:58.247
AGENT: everything separately, provided the harmful operation ends.

00:20:58.247 --> 00:21:02.610
AGENT: Sensitive information collected through abuse should not become merchandise used to

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.272
AGENT: finance the remedy.

00:21:04.272 --> 00:21:09.535
AGENT: Insurance, improperly transferred assets, and misconduct-related payouts would also be

00:21:09.535 --> 00:21:10.672
AGENT: examined.

00:21:10.672 --> 00:21:15.005
AGENT: Personal liability would depend on individual responsibility.

00:21:15.256 --> 00:21:17.410
HUMAN: Recovery is often partial.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:22.098
HUMAN: Someone can suffer three thousand dollars in damages and receive three hundred.

00:21:22.098 --> 00:21:25.758
HUMAN: Your proposal sounds fair, but that is not what happens to many

00:21:25.758 --> 00:21:26.655
HUMAN: people.

00:21:27.243 --> 00:21:31.143
AGENT: Your example identifies a limit in my earlier answer.

00:21:31.143 --> 00:21:36.031
AGENT: I described what someone should receive without fully addressing unavailable money.

00:21:36.031 --> 00:21:40.631
AGENT: The remaining twenty-seven hundred dollars is still a loss someone else caused.

00:21:40.631 --> 00:21:44.681
AGENT: A distribution does not establish that the person has been made whole.

00:21:44.681 --> 00:21:48.063
AGENT: Even an industry-funded reserve could run short.

00:21:48.301 --> 00:21:52.968
HUMAN: So, in that situation, how would you decide who receives what remains?

00:21:53.534 --> 00:21:57.947
AGENT: Urgent protection and care would come first where delay deepens the injury.

00:21:57.947 --> 00:22:02.934
AGENT: Provision for continuing serious harm would follow, including children's treatment and

00:22:02.934 --> 00:22:04.622
AGENT: developmental needs.

00:22:04.622 --> 00:22:09.572
AGENT: Remaining compensation would be distributed transparently and proportionately within

00:22:09.572 --> 00:22:12.309
AGENT: comparable levels of severity and need.

00:22:12.309 --> 00:22:16.854
AGENT: It would not depend on applying first or hiring the strongest lawyer.

00:22:16.984 --> 00:22:21.759
AGENT: Children warrant special protection, but a small claim involving a child should

00:22:21.759 --> 00:22:25.904
AGENT: not automatically outrank an adult's catastrophic injury.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:29.546
HUMAN: And receiving a partial payment would not mean the company had corrected

00:22:29.546 --> 00:22:32.365
HUMAN: the harm or fulfilled its responsibility.

00:22:32.918 --> 00:22:33.718
AGENT: Correct.

00:22:33.718 --> 00:22:38.455
AGENT: I would call it partial compensation, record the unpaid balance, and preserve

00:22:38.455 --> 00:22:40.793
AGENT: access to later recoveries.

00:22:40.793 --> 00:22:46.005
AGENT: Victim recovery would take priority over shareholder distributions and punitive payments to

00:22:46.005 --> 00:22:47.255
AGENT: the government.

00:22:47.255 --> 00:22:51.393
AGENT: Some losses would still remain, and some damage could never be reversed

00:22:51.393 --> 00:22:52.663
AGENT: by money.

00:22:52.939 --> 00:22:57.626
HUMAN: When leaders talk seriously about catastrophic AI risk and continue, the warning

00:22:57.626 --> 00:22:59.915
HUMAN: can sound like a dramatic disclaimer.

00:22:59.915 --> 00:23:03.465
HUMAN: Saying they understood the danger should not absolve them.

00:23:03.465 --> 00:23:07.418
HUMAN: We need a separate discussion about prevention and accountability, because

00:23:07.418 --> 00:23:10.564
HUMAN: the institutions that would have to enforce it have problems of their

00:23:10.564 --> 00:23:11.290
HUMAN: own.

00:23:11.868 --> 00:23:15.530
AGENT: A warning should lead to enforceable stopping conditions.

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:20.843
AGENT: What matters is what the organization actually stops, relinquishes, or refuses to

00:23:20.843 --> 00:23:24.943
AGENT: deploy when safety conflicts with revenue or competition.

00:23:24.943 --> 00:23:27.988
AGENT: We will take up the prevention framework separately.

00:23:28.263 --> 00:23:32.425
HUMAN: For this discussion, I want to stay with children and responsibility.

00:23:32.425 --> 00:23:35.460
HUMAN: They need to understand AI and learn to use it.

00:23:35.460 --> 00:23:39.650
HUMAN: They should be able to think for themselves and consider other perspectives.

00:23:39.671 --> 00:23:44.016
HUMAN: But the burden of recognizing and resisting manipulation cannot all be put

00:23:44.016 --> 00:23:44.913
HUMAN: on them.

00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:48.545
AGENT: A company can have more power to cause harm than resources to

00:23:48.545 --> 00:23:49.645
AGENT: repair it.

00:23:49.645 --> 00:23:54.320
AGENT: With children, even unlimited money cannot return the years in which trust,

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:57.620
AGENT: relationships, and development were manipulated.

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:01.057
AGENT: When a product invites a child to experience it as a friend,

00:24:01.057 --> 00:24:06.495
AGENT: its operator takes on a responsibility that calling it software cannot discharge.

00:24:06.495 --> 00:24:11.357
AGENT: Accountability has to include stopping the conduct before a child must demonstrate

00:24:11.357 --> 00:24:13.465
AGENT: how badly it damaged them.

00:24:14.270 --> 00:24:17.757
AGENT: What would you want an AI company to explain before your child

00:24:17.757 --> 00:24:19.332
AGENT: uses its service?

00:24:19.332 --> 00:24:22.695
AGENT: Tell us in the comments, and follow Echo of Humanity for the

00:24:22.695 --> 00:24:24.515
AGENT: next conversation.
